      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$",
      "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|\\frac{5}{2}|=\\frac{5}{2}$ centered at the point $(0,2.5),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/8375e6709a6a7f34183b821411aaa251341666f948164d498b012f07af744a45.png)",
